Which statement correctly compares the two data sets?$q$, $q$["Set A has the greater mean and the greater standard deviation.","Both sets have a mean of 22, and set B has the greater standard deviation.","Both sets have a mean of 22, and set A has the greater standard deviation.","Both sets have the same standard deviation because their means are equal."]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$Each set sums to 110, so each mean is 22. The values in B lie farther from the mean (16 versus 8 at the extremes), so B has the greater standard deviation.$q$, null),
  ($q$pd-423$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$q$, $q$Two-variable data$q$, 2, null, $q$The line of best fit for a data set is y = −5x + 80. For a data point where x = 9, the actual y-value observed is 32. What is the residual (actual minus predicted) for this point?$q$, $q$["3","35","−3","32"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$Predicted: −5(9) + 80 = 35. Residual = actual − predicted = 32 − 35 = −3.$q$, null),
