  ($q$pd-545$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$q$, $q$Probability$q$, 2, null, $q$The probability that a certain event occurs on any given day is 1/4, independent of other days. What is the probability that the event occurs on at least one of two consecutive days?$q$, $q$["7/16","1/16","1/2","3/4"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The event fails both days with probability ((3)/4)² = 9/16. So P(at least one) = 1 − 9/16 = 7/16.$q$, null),
  ($q$pd-546$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$q$, $q$Ratios and proportions$q$, 1, null, $q$The ratio of x to y is 1:4, and the ratio of y to z is 8:3. What is the ratio of x to z?$q$, $q$["3:5","1:3","2:3","4:3"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$x:y = 1:4 = 2:8. Since y:z = 8:3, matching the y-terms gives x:y:z = 2:8:3, so x:z = 2:3.$q$, null),
