  ($q$pd-549$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$q$, $q$Evaluating statistical claims$q$, 2, null, $q$In a study, patients with mild headaches were randomly assigned to either receive a new pain reliever or not receive it. The group that received a new pain reliever showed a statistically significant improvement in reported pain. Which conclusion is best supported by the study?$q$, $q$["A new pain reliever improves reported pain for everyone, regardless of group.","Neither group's reported pain changed.","A new pain reliever likely caused the improvement in reported pain for patients with mild headaches like those in the study.","Reported pain and a new pain reliever are correlated, but no causal conclusion is possible."]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$Random assignment supports a causal conclusion, but only for populations similar to the participants.$q$, null),
