  ($q$pd-635$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$q$, $q$Two-variable data$q$, 2, null, $q$A line of best fit for a scatterplot is y = 1.5x + 76, where x is the number of employees and y is the monthly output. Which of the following is the best interpretation of the number 1.5 in this context?$q$, $q$["When the number of employees is 0, the predicted monthly output is 1.5.","The monthly output increases by 1.5 percent each time.","For each 1-unit increase in the number of employees, the predicted monthly output increases by 1.5.","The number of employees is predicted to be 1.5 when the monthly output is 76."]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$The slope is the predicted change in y for each 1-unit increase in x.$q$, null),
  ($q$pd-636$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$q$, $q$Percentages$q$, 1, null, $q$The price of a jacket decreased from $50 to $40. By what percent did the price decrease? (Round to the nearest whole percent.)$q$, $q$["25%","30%","15%","20%"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$Percent change = |40 − 50| / 50 × 100 = 10/50 × 100 ≈ 20%.$q$, null),
  ($q$pd-637$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$q$, $q$Rates and units$q$, 2, null, $q$One hose can fill a tank in 30 hours, and a second hose can fill the same tank in 20 hours. Working together, how many hours will the two hoses take to fill the tank?$q$, $q$["50","13","12","10"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$The combined rate is 1/30 + 1/20 = 50/600 of the tank per hour, so the time is 600/50 = 12 hours.$q$, null),
