  ($q$pd-650$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$q$, $q$Conditional probability$q$, 2, null, $q$A survey asked 97 students whether they prefer online or in-person classes. Of the 48 first-year students, 18 prefer online classes. Of the 49 upper-year students, 38 prefer online classes. If a student who prefers online classes is chosen at random, what is the probability that the student is a first-year student?$q$, $q$["3/8","9/28","19/28","18/97"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$56 students prefer online classes, and 18 of them are first-year students, so the probability is 18/56 = 9/28.$q$, null),
