  ($q$pd-653$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$q$, $q$Percentages$q$, 2, null, $q$A store discounts an item by 10%, and then takes an additional 20% off the discounted price. The two discounts together are equivalent to a single discount of what percent?$q$, $q$["25%","28%","10%","30%"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$The price becomes 0.9 × 0.8 = 0.72 of the original, which is a discount of 28%.$q$, null),
