  ($q$pd-717$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$q$, $q$Evaluating statistical claims$q$, 2, null, $q$A researcher randomly selected 300 adults from a city's voter list and asked whether they support a new park. Of them, 186 said yes. Which conclusion is best supported by this information?$q$, $q$["Exactly 62% of all adults in the country support new parks.","Every voter in the city supports the park.","Building the park will cause voter turnout to increase.","About 62% of the city's registered voters likely support the new park."]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$The sample was randomly selected from the city's voter list, so the result (186/300 = 62%) can be generalized only to that population, and only approximately. The other conclusions overreach to a different population, claim certainty, or assert causation.$q$, null),
